findings.finding:
The census is specified only for `pytest.mark.timeout(N)` decorators and `pytestmark = pytest.mark.timeout(N)` assignments. Several other literal spellings would pass unchecked, letting a sub-floor marker evade the guard the AC relies on:
- the keyword form `pytest.mark.timeout(timeout=3)`;
- list or tuple `pytestmark = [pytest.mark.timeout(3), ...]`;
- `from pytest import mark` / `mark.timeout(3)` aliasing;
- `pytest.param(..., marks=pytest.mark.timeout(3))`.
